Creating chain of events. Event could be canseled or fired. 
evt2 follows evt1 + 0.3 seconds
1. evt1 fired -> wait 0.3 seconds -> fire evt2
2. evt1 canceled -> evt2 canceled

Event placed inside scope (script). If we return from script, events killed (canceled or just unsubscribed quietly)

example
```
warning about attack1 (animation)
t1 = 0.3 seconds
create parry collider for attack1 after t1 end
t2 = 0.4 seconds after t1 end
remove parry collider for attack1 after t2 end
send intention to executing attack1 after t2 end

warning about attack2 (animation) after t1 end
t3 = 0.3 seconds after t1 end
create parry collider for atack2 after t3 end
t4 = 0.4 seconds after t3 end
remove parry collider for attack2 after t4 end
send intention to executing attack2 after t4 end

I want it look like

t1 = timer(0.3)
t2 = t1.then(0.4)
t3 = t1.then(0.3)
t4 = t3.then(0.4)

attack1_warning = someWarningConstructor(
	func(ctx)
		--yields every update to draw until t2 end or attack1 canceled
	end
)
attack1_parry = someParryContrusctor(form, e.t.c...
	func(ctx) --called if parried
		--yields every update for logic until some time (or event without yielding and execute all in one frame)
	end
